-- Source module: Solutions.KIL3Level
/-!
# KIL3: one Prop. 11 level (`levelR`) as an IL procedure, bit data

The level of `AModelProp11.levelR` over `ZMod 2` (the bit network), with the bits stored as the
integers `0, 1` (`enc2`).  The code is

1. `D ← D − H` (`subSteps`, the KIL2 runner, coefficients `±1`);
2. the cyclic row split into the `W` streams (`bwdP`, KILRow), the streams one after the other on
   stack `0`;
3. the network (`netC`, KIL3Net): per gate the frame changes `Φ_X` of the touched streams in
   place (the Lemma 10 steps of `X`, shifts by any implemented shift code, interchanges by calls of
   the child procedures), then the pointwise gate (sums mod 2); finally the frame changes to the
   output labels;
4. the routing: stream `w` ← stream `ρ w` (`rebuildC`);
5. the row merge (`fwdP`);
6. `D ← H − D` (`flipSteps`).

Main results: `levelR_run` (the level code computes `levelR` for any shift code correct on
integer arrays, cost `levelCI`), `levelCI_le` (`levelCI ≤ lvlK·(V+1)·(Bb+2)² + nShift·cS +
rankSum C·(c₀ + 2)`), `levelR_il_small` (KIL2 shift codes, units `±1, ±k, ±k⁻¹`, `k ≤ 20`).
The children are only required on the interchanges `H_i ↔ D_j` (`edgeSteps_swap_HD`).
